#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# airy_ai_prime

#% text
# `airy_ai_prime(x)` gives the derivative `Ai'(x)` of the Airy function.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `airy_ai_prime(0)` is `-3^(-1/3)/gamma(1/3)`. Machine numbers, balls and complex numbers give numerical values.

#% item
# Its derivative is `x*airy_ai(x)`, from the Airy equation (DLMF 9.2.1).

#% item
# `airy_ai_prime` is listable.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
airy_ai_prime(0)
#% output
#= -3^(2/3)/(3*gamma(1/3))

#% cell
airy_ai_prime(1.0)
#% output
#= -0.1591474412967932

#% cell
airy_ai_prime(-3.0)
#% output
#= 0.3145837692165988

#% cell
n(airy_ai_prime(1), 30)
#% output
#= -0.1591474412967932127875002524972297

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# A complex argument:

#% cell
airy_ai_prime(1.0*im)
#% output
#= -0.4324926598418071 + 0.09804785622924324im

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# The derivative:

#% cell
d(airy_ai_prime(x), x)
#% output
#= x*airy_ai(x)

#% text
# A difference quotient of `airy_ai`:

#% cell
(airy_ai(1.0 + 1.0e-6) - airy_ai(1.0 - 1.0e-6))/2.0e-6 - airy_ai_prime(1.0)
#% output
#= 1.9330648193260913e-12

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `airy_ai`, `airy_bi_prime`, `airy_bi`
